A series of Joey support made by a collective of people and brought together by DRikkets1991. 

Currently in the works. 

Total card count = 26

Projected card count = 66

Here's the card list:
1.) Red-Eyes Salamandra Dragon (FIRE/DRAGON/FUSION/LEVEL 8)
    "Red-Eyes Black Dragon" + 1 FIRE monster	
    Must first be Fusion Summoned or Special Summoned from your Extra Deck by sending the above cards from your hand or field to the GY. 
    Your opponent cannot send cards from their hand to the GY to activate effects. 
    This card can attack all monsters your opponent controls, once each. 
    When this card is Special Summoned: You can send 1 "Red-Eyes" or "Salamandra" card from your Deck to the GY; add 1 "Red-Eyes" or "Salamandra" card from your Deck to your hand with a different Card Type (Monster, Spell, or Trap) than that sent card. 
    You can only use this effect of "Red-Eyes Salamandra Dragon" once per turn. 
    Once per turn, at the end of the Damage Step, if this card battled: You can target 1 Spell in your GY; add it to your hand.
2.) Red-Eyes Darkness Flare Metal Dragon (DARK/DRAGON/XYZ/RANK 7) --Mergo
    3 level 7 "Red-Eyes" monsters	
    Unaffected by your opponent's card effects while it has material. 
    While this card has material, each time your opponent activates a card or effect, inflict 700 damage to them immediately after it resolves. 
    Once per turn (Quick-Effect): You can detach 1 material from this card, then target 1 "Red-Eyes" card in your GY; Special Summon it (if a monster), Set it to your Spell & Trap Zone (if a Spell/Trap), or add it to your hand.
3.) The Gambler's Fate (NORMAL SPELL)
    Roll 2 six-sided die. 
    Excavate the top 6 cards of your Deck and add cards excavated this way equal to the lower die result, or if both die rolled the same number, add all excavated cards to your hand, then shuffle the remaining cards into the Deck. 
    If you excavated a "Red-Eyes" or a Dragon monster(s), you can choose to Special Summon 1 of those monsters instead of adding it to your hand, and if you do, you can only Special Summon "Red-Eyes" monsters or monsters that mention "Flame Swordsman" or "Dark Time Wizard" for the rest of this turn. 
    You can only activate "The Gambler's Fate" once per turn.
4.) Lord of the Red-Eyes (FIRE/DRAGON/EFFECT/LEVEL 7)
    Cannot be Normal Summoned/Set. 
    Must first be Special Summoned (from your hand or GY) by sending 1 level 7 or higher "Red-Eyes" monster from your hand or face-up field to the GY. 
    You can only Special Summon "Lord of the Red-Eyes" once per turn this way. 
    Your opponent cannot target this card with card effects, and if it is equipped with an Equip Spell, it cannot be destroyed by battle. 
    Up to twice per turn, when a card or effect is activated (Quick-Effect): You can target 1 card on the field; destroy it, then if it was a monster, inflict damage to your opponent equal to its original ATK. 
    You can send an Equip Spell equipped to "Lord of the Red-Eyes" to the GY; add 1 "Red-Eyes" Field or Continuous Spell from your Deck to your hand. 
    You can only use this effect of "Lord of the Red-Eyes" once per turn.
5.) Megacyber with Eyes of Red (DARK/WARRIOR/EFFECT/LEVEL 6)
    (This card is always treated as a "Red-Eyes" card)	
    If you control no monsters, you can Special Summon this card (from your hand). 
    You can only Special Summon "Megacyber with Eyes of Red" once per turn this way. 
    You can only use each of the following effects of "Megacyber with Eyes of Red" once per turn. 
    If this card is Special Summoned while your opponent controls more monsters than you do: You can Special Summon level 7 or lower "Red-Eyes" monsters with different names from your hand or GY until you control an equal number of monsters. 
    You cannot Special Summon monsters from the Extra Deck the turn you activate this effect, except for Fusion or Xyz Monsters. 
    If this card is sent to the GY: You can target 1 "Red-Eyes" Normal Gemini Monster you control; it is treated as an Effect Monster and it gains its effect(s).
6.) Red-Eyes Shadow Hunter (EARTH/WARRIOR/EFFECT/LEVEL 7)
    If a "Red-Eyes" or Warrior monster you control destroys an opponent's monster by battle: You can Special Summon this card (from your hand). 
    Each time this card destroys an opponent's monster by battle, equip that monster from the GY to this card as an Equip Spell with this effect. 
    ● The equipped monster gains 300 ATK/DEF.	
    If this card destroys an opponent's monster by battle: It can attack again in a row. 
    If your opponent takes effect damage while this card is in your GY: You can Special Summon this card, and if you do, inflict 1200 damage to your opponent.
7.) Red-Eyes Black Dragon, Dragon of Limitless Potential (DARK/DRAGON/EFFECT/LEVEL 7)
    This card's name becomes "Red-Eyes Black Dragon" while on the field. 
    You can Special Summon this card from your hand by Tributing 1 monster from your hand or field, then inflict damage to your opponent equal to this card's original ATK. 
    You can only Special Summon "Red Eyes Black Dragon, Dragon of Limitless Potential" once per turn this way. 
    You can only use each of the following effects of "Red-Eyes Black Dragon, Dragon of Limitless Potential" once per turn.
    When this card is Special Summoned: You can take 1 card that mentions "Red-Eyes Black Dragon", "Flame Swordsman", "Dark Time Wizard", "Max Metalmorph" or "The Claw of Hermos" from your Deck, except "Red-Eyes Black Dragon, Dragon of Limitless Potential", and either add it to your hand, or if it is a monster, you can Special Summon it, also, you cannot Special Summon monsters from the Extra Deck for the rest of this turn, except Fusion or Xyz Monsters. 
    When your opponent activates a card or effect (Quick Effect): You can Fusion Summon 1 Fusion Monster that lists a "Red-Eyes" monster as material from your Extra Deck by shuffling its materials from your field or GY into the Deck, including this card. 
    During the End Phase, if this card is in the GY because it was sent there this turn: You can Special Summon it, and if you do, increase this its ATK by 600 (this remains even after this card leaves the field and returns).
8.) Flash Flame Swordsman (FIRE/WARRIOR/EFFECT/LEVEL 5)
    This card's name becomes "Flame Swordsman" while on the field or in the GY. 
    You can only use each of the following effects of "Flash Flame Swordsman" once per turn. 
    If this card is in your hand: You can target 1 face-up monster your opponent controls; switch the original ATK and DEF of that monster until the end of this turn, then immediately after this effect resolves, Normal Summon this card without Tributing. 
    During your Main Phase or your opponent's Battle Phase (Quick-Effect): You can activate the following effect; Fusion Summon 1 Fusion Monster that mentions "Dark Time Wizard" or "Flame Swordsman" from your Extra Deck, using monsters from your hand and/or field as material, including this card.
9.) Red-Eyes Black Flame Swordsman (DARK/WARRIOR/EFFECT/LEVEL 5)
    While face-up on the field, this card is also a FIRE monster. 
    Gains 700 ATK for each card equipped to it. 
    You can only use each of the following effects of "Red-Eyes Black Flame Swordsman" once per turn. 
    If you control a "Red-Eyes" or Warrior monster: You can Special Summon this card from your hand, and if you do, add 1 card that mentions "Dark Time Wizard" or "Flame Swordsman" from your Deck to your hand. 
    You can banish 1 card equipped to this card; Special Summon 1 monster that mentions "Dark Time Wizard" or "Flame Swordsman" from your hand. 
    Up to twice per turn, when a card or effect is activated that targets this card, or when an opponent's monster declares an attack (Quick-Effect): You can negate the activation or attack, and if you do, equip 1 card your opponent controls to this card as an Equip Spell. 
    If this card leaves the field: You can target 1 FIRE Warrior or DARK Dragon monster in your GY, except "Red-Eyes Black Flame Swordsman"; Special Summon it.
10.) Jinzo, Black Dragon Armored (DARK/MACHINE/FUSION/LEVEL 8)
    "Jinzo" + 1 "Red-Eyes" monster	
    (This card is also a Dragon monster)	
    Must first be Fusion Summoned. 
    "Red-Eyes" and level 5 or higher Machine monsters you control are unaffected by your opponent's Trap effects. 
    You can only use each of the following effects of "Jinzo, Black Dragon Armored" once per turn. 
    When this card is Special Summoned: You can target any number of Trap Cards in your GY; shuffle them into the Deck, then if "Max Metalmorph" was shuffled into the Deck by this effect, you can shuffle an equal number of Set cards your opponent controls into the Deck. 
    At the start of your Battle Phase: You can take control of the monster your opponent controls with the highest ATK (your choice, if tied) until the end of the Battle Phase, also it must attack this turn, if able.
